$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the acid-catalyzed Paal–Knorr pyrrole
cyclocondensation Silica-supported antimony(III) chloride (0.30 g, 0.10
mmol of loaded SbCl3) was well stirred in hexane (5 mL) for a few
minutes. Primary amine (3 mmol) and hexane-2,5- dione (4.3 mmol) were
then added, and the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 1 h. The
progress of the reaction was monitored by thin layer chromatography or
gas chromatography. Upon the completion of the reaction, the mixture was
filtered off and the solid was washed with dichloromethane. The combined
organic phase was evaporated under reduced pressure and afforded the
crude product. It was passed through a short column of silica gel [eluted
with ethyl acetate/hexane (1:8)]. The pure products.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Paal-Knorr pyrrole cyclocondensation, silica-supported SbCl3 used as
catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Silica-supported antimony(III) chloride as a mild and reusable catalyst
for the Paal-Knorr pyrrole synthesis
