$DATUM 104-15-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A. General procedure for the
microwave-accelerated synthesis of 2,5-dimethyl-1-aryl-1H-pyrroles (6).
2,5-Hexandione (4) (1 mmol), the appropriate aniline 5a-x (1.2 equiv) and
p-toluenesulfonic acid bound with silica gel (0.4 equiv) were mixed in an
oven dried pressure vial with a magnetic stirrer bar. The vessel was
placed in a microwave oven and heated (180 °C, 15-20 min) under microwave
irradiation (0-400 W at 2.45 GHz). After stirring for a further 15 min at
room temperature the reaction mixture was filtered and the residual
silica washed with DCM (10 mL). The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure to give the corresponding 2,5-dimethyl-1-aryl-1H-pyrrole 6a-x
(80-90% yield, purity &gt;95% by LCMS).
2,5-Dimethyl-1-(2-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-1H-pyrrole (6a). Prepared
following General Procedure A to give 6a.
1-Benzyl-2,5-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole (6x). Prepared following General
Procedure A to give 6x. Brown semi-solid, (2.9 g, 90%). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.41 (m, 3H, J = 7.45 Hz), 7.01 (d, 2H, J = 7.75 Hz), 5.98 (d,
2H, J = 10.6), 5.12 (d, 2H, J = 10.3. Hz), 2.25 (d, 6H, J = 10.4 Hz). MS
(ESI): calcd for C13H16N, 186.0512; m/z found 186.1174 (M+1)100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (0W-400W), solid-supported catalyst, no solvent,
pressure vial used, Paal-Knorr pyrrole synthesis, silica gel support used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery and Structure-Activity Relationships of Pyrrolone Antimalarials
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Murugesan, Dinakaran; Mital, Alka; Kaiser, Marcel; Shackleford, David M.;
Morizzi, Julia; Katneni, Kasiram; Campbell, Michael; Hudson, Alan;
Charman, Susan A.; Yeates, Clive; Gilbert, Ian H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Medicinal Chemistry (2013), 56(7), 2975-2990

