$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
compounds (3a-3s). 1-(4-Chloro-phenyl)-2, 5-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole (3a). A
mixture of 2,5-hexadione (1, 1.0 mmol), 4-chlorophenylamine (2, 1.0
mmol), and α-amylase from hog pancreas (30 mg) was introduced to a test
tube (10 mL), 2 mL CH3OH then the mixture was horizontally shake (160
rpm) at 50 °C. The solution was then filtered off by paper and the
solvent was evaporated. The residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography with an eluent consisting of petroleum/ethyl acetate (5:1
v/v). 5-(2,5-Dimethyl-pyrrol-1-yl)-3-methyl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazole (3s);
Yield: 90%; Reaction condition: 2 h. M.p. 139-141 °C. IR (KBr) (νmax,
cm-1): 2925, 1658, 1413, 1260, 1093. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.91
(s, 6H, CH3), 2.41 (s, 3H, CH3), 5.88 (s, 2H, CH), 6.21 (s, 2H, CH),
6.98-7.00 (m, 2H, ArH), 7.18-7.27 (m, 3H, ArH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM biotransformation, enzymic, alpha-amylase from hog pancreas used,
Paal-Knorr reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A novel enzyme-catalyzed synthesis of N-substituted pyrrole derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zheng, Hui; Shi, Qiaoyue; Du, Kui; Mei, Yijia; Zhang, Pengfei
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Molecular Diversity (2013), 17(2), 245-250

